# index-page.js — Homepage Behavior

## Layman's terms

The JavaScript that makes the homepage work: mobile menu toggle, holiday countdown, and any other interactive bits. Runs when the homepage loads.

## Medium understanding

Extracted from Thrive Architect export. Handles mobile menu (toggle, overlay close, link click close), video banner countdown, and other homepage-specific behavior. DOM-ready pattern; no framework. IDs/classes follow Thrive export conventions (sec-mobile-toggle, sec-menu-wrapper, etc.).

## Advanced

- **Scope:** Homepage (Pages/index/)
- **Pattern:** DOMContentLoaded, IIFE for isolation
- **Deps:** None; vanilla JS
